up with our DraftKings NFL Week 12 cheat sheet identifying the best stacks and values","published":"2026-11-27T11:46:44.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/fantasy/football/story/_/id/50607390/draftkings-nfl-dfs-values-week-12","type":"Story","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Best friends Pat Surtain II, Jaylen Waddle ecstatic about reuniting with Broncos","description":"Surtain and Waddle bonded immediately at Alabama six years ago and have embraced the chance to play together again in Denver on a team with Super Bowl hopes.","published":"2026-11-27T11:00:22.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/story/_/id/50595313/pat-surtain-ii-jaylen-waddle-broncos-alabama-best-friends","type":"Story","byline":"Jeff Legwold","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Why the Seahawks are turning back to quarterback Sam Darnold vs. the 49ers","description":"Drew Lock has been 'fantastic' filling in for Darnold, who has struggled with injuries but is on track to face 9-1 San Francisco on Sunday.","published":"2026-11-27T12:02:29.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/story/_/id/50609180/why-seahawks-starting-qb-sam-darnold-49ers-week-12","type":"Story","byline":"Brady Henderson","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"2027 NFL draft order projections for Round 1, chances for top pick, more","description":"ESPN's Football Power Index projects the 2027 NFL draft order for Round 1, complete with each team's chances to pick in the top five, in the top 10 and at No. 1.","published":"2026-11-27T11:00:02.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/draft2027/story/_/id/49794361/2027-nfl-draft-order-projections-first-round-picks","type":"Story","byline":"ESPN staff","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Can the 49ers lock up the NFC West after exceeding preseason expectations?","description":"The 49ers are 9-1, and two of their next three games are against the Seahawks (6-4) and Rams (7-4) at home.","published":"2026-11-27T11:00:13.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/story/_/id/50582755/san-francisco-49ers-nfc-west-playoffs-seeding","type":"Story","byline":"Nick Wagoner","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"NFL Week 12 preview: Picks, predictions, schedule, betting odds, fantasy tips","description":"Seahawks vs. 49ers? Kirk Cousins against Atlanta? There are 12 more games in Week 12, and we have picks, predictions and more for all of them.","published":"2026-11-27T11:48:57.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/story/_/id/50587851/week-12-picks-predictions-schedule-fantasy-odds-2026","type":"Story","byline":"NFL Nation, Pamela Maldonado, Eric Moody and Seth Walder","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"2026 NFL playoff picture: AFC, NFC seed projections, chances to make postseason","description":"We're looking ahead to how the 14-team playoff picture could line up -- and who will win divisions -- en route to the Super Bowl.","published":"2026-11-27T11:00:08.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/story/_/id/49745176/2026-nfl-playoff-predictions-afc-nfc-odds-super-bowl","type":"Story","byline":"ESPN staff","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Rashee Rice, Chiefs believe he caught pivotal 3rd-down pass late vs. Bills","description":"WR Rashee Rice -- along with several members of the Chiefs -- felt he caught the ball on a pivotal third-down pass with less than two minutes left at the Bills.","published":"2026-11-27T08:17:16.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/story/_/id/50609968/rashee-rice-chiefs-believe-caught-pivotal-3rd-pass","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Nate Taylor","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Bills QB Josh Allen struggles vs. Chiefs in 'grossest' conditions","description":"The Bills won their 10th game of the season Thursday vs. the Chiefs, but QB Josh Allen struggled in the weather, passing for only 81 yards.","published":"2026-11-27T07:57:30.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/story/_/id/50609813/bills-qb-josh-allen-struggles-vs-chiefs-grossest-conditions","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Nick Suss","source":"ESPN"}],"wiki":{"title":"Tay Martin","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tay_Martin","description":"American football player (born 1997)","touched":"2026-11-26T23:15:20Z","intro":"Davontavean Martin (born December 14, 1997) is an American professional football wide receiver for the Detroit Lions of the National Football League (NFL). He played college football for the Washington State Cougars and Oklahoma State Cowboys. Martin has also been a member of the San Francisco 49ers, Tennessee Titans, Washington Commanders, and the UFL's Columbus Aviators. He was signed as an undrafted free agent by the 49ers following the 2022 NFL draft.","sections":[{"key":"career","title":"Professional career","text":"SAN FRANCISCO 49ERS\nOn April 30, 2022, Martin signed with the San Francisco 49ers as an undrafted free agent. He was released during final roster cutdowns on August 30. Martin was signed to the team's practice squad the following day. He signed a reserve/future contract with the 49ers on January 31, 2023.\nOn August 29, 2023, Martin was waived by the 49ers and re-signed to the practice squad. He signed a reserve/future contract with San Francisco on February 13, 2024.\nMartin was waived by the 49ers on August 27, 2024, and re-signed to the practice squad. On September 3, Martin was released from the practice squad.\n\nTENNESSEE TITANS\nOn September 10, 2024, Martin was signed to the Tennessee Titans' practice squad. He was promoted to the active roster on January 4, 2025. In a 23-14 Week 18 loss to the Houston Texans, Martin made his first career reception on a 49-yard touchdown pass from quarterback Will Levis.\nOn May 7, 2025, Martin was waived/injured by the Titans and reverted to the injured reserve the following day. He was waived again on May 14.\n\nWASHINGTON COMMANDERS\nMartin signed with the Washington Commanders on July 23, 2025, and was released on August 26. Martin re-signed with their practice squad on September 16. He was elevated to the active roster for Weeks 4, 5, and 6, but was released from the practice squad on October 17.\n\nCOLUMBUS AVIATORS\nOn January 14, 2026, Martin was selected by the Columbus Aviators of the United Football League (UFL).\n\nDETROIT LIONS\nOn June 16, 2026, Martin signed with the Detroit Lions. For his contributions to special teams in the Week 1 win against the Saints, he received a game ball."},{"key":"personal","title":"Personal life","text":"Tay Martin is engaged to Morgan Pitre. They have two daughters, Reign and Valley."}],"wikidataId":"Q114282822","social":{}},"transactions":[{"date":"2026-07-22","text":"Waived WR Kyre Duplessis. Signed WRs Tarik Black, Lucky Jackson and Tay Martin to contracts. Placed WR Kendrick Law on injured reserve."},{"date":"2026-06-16","text":"Signed WRs Tay Martin, Tarik Black and Lucky Jackson to contracts. Placed WR Kendrick Law on injured reserve. Waived WR Kyre Duplessis."}],"links":{"espn":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/4245144","pfr":"https://www.pro-football-reference.com/players/M/MartTa00.htm","pff":"https://www.pff.com/nfl/players/tay-martin/61811","otc":"https://overthecap.com/player/tay-martin/10555","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tay_Martin"},"insights":["2026 cap number of $1.0M is the 44th-largest on the roster.","Contract expires after this season.","Entered the league in 2022 as an undrafted free agent."]}